750.1200 & 1220 - A) hole was observed in the floor along the wall below the paper towel dispenser in the women's room. Re-seal the floor where disrepair is present in the women's room.

B) Coving was loose/missing along the floor to wall juncture at the south wall next to the register. Debris accumulation was observed in the area. Clean the aforementioned area and re-seal the floor to wall juncture.

C) Floors were soiled in the following areas:
1. between counter and wall at drink counter (general buildup/debris);
2. along walls/in corners of walkin cooler (food/general buildup);
3. along walls/in corners of walkin freezer (food/debris);
4. under 3 part sink (black buildup along floor to wall juncture);   and
5. behind bread oven and holding cart (crumbs/debris along floor to wall juncture).
Clean the floor in the aforementioned areas.

Floors must be in good repair, constructed to facilitate easy cleaning, and maintained clean. Junctures between walls and floors shall be coved and sealed (see general comments).
